      "steps": [
        {
          "step_number": 1,
          "title": "Step 1",
          "instruction": "Raspeballer & (Optional) Salted Meat"
        },
        {
          "step_number": 2,
          "title": "Step 2",
          "instruction": "\u25a2"
        },
        {
          "step_number": 3,
          "title": "Step 3",
          "instruction": "If you're making pork knuckle, cook it in simmering water for about 3 hours, until the meat falls from the bone. Remove the pork and save the broth to cook the raspeballer."
        },
        {
          "step_number": 4,
          "title": "Step 4",
          "instruction": "\u25a2"
        },
        {
          "step_number": 5,
          "title": "Step 5",
          "instruction": "Boil the boiled potatoes and peel once cooled. Also peel the raw potatoes, and then grate them or run them through a food processor. Use a paper towel to remove some of the moisture from the grated potatoes."
        },
        {
          "step_number": 6,
          "title": "Step 6",
          "instruction": "\u25a2"
        },
        {
          "step_number": 7,
          "title": "Step 7",
          "instruction": "Mash the boiled potatoes in a potato ricer or with a masher. Make sure there are no lumps. Add the grated raw potatoes to the mashed potatoes in a large mixing bowl and stir together. Add the barley flour, all purpose flour, and salt and mix together with your hands until the mixture is fully blended."
        },
        {
          "step_number": 8,
          "title": "Step 8",
          "instruction": "\u25a2"
        },
        {
          "step_number": 9,
          "title": "Step 9",
          "instruction": "You can cook the raspeballer in either vegetable or beef broth, or if you're making pork knuckle, cook them in the broth from the pork knuckle. Bring the broth to a very light simmer \u2013 you don't want it to fully boil because then the raspeballer might break apart."
        },
        {
          "step_number": 10,
          "title": "Step 10",
          "instruction": "\u25a2"
        },
        {
          "step_number": 11,
          "title": "Step 11",
          "instruction": "Use a tablespoon dipped in cold water to shape each raspeball in your hand. Try to make them as smooth as possible and then gently drop them into the simmering broth. Dip the tablespoon in a bowl of cold water between each raspeball."
        },
        {
          "step_number": 12,
          "title": "Step 12",
          "instruction": "\u25a2"
        },
        {
